schema: "0.4"
id: geopandas-02-dense-layer-stress
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: geopandas
category: geospatial-and-mapping
variant: dense-layer-stress
references:
  - "references/fim/overview/geospatial-math-scientific/geopandas.md"
  - "references/fim/solution/geopandas.md"
prompt:
  system: |-
    Generate production-quality GeoPandas assets for FIM geospatial-and-mapping evaluation. Follow the referenced solution APIs and return only the requested source artifact.
  text: |-
    Create a GeoPandas dense layer stress case asset for the geospatial-and-mapping category.

    Scenario:
    Create a dense metropolitan mobility stress test with many synthetic GPS pings, stops, zones, and temporal or categorical attributes. The artifact must use the solution-appropriate clustering, aggregation, tiling, spatial index, WebGL, or sampling strategy instead of naively drawing every feature.

    Implementation requirements:
    - Use native GeoPandas patterns from the referenced overview and solution docs; do not replace the requested solution with a generic screenshot or unrelated map library.
    - Use GeoPandas APIs such as GeoDataFrame, GeoSeries, read_file, to_crs, estimate_utm_crs, sjoin, overlay, dissolve, clip, make_valid, spatial index use, GeoParquet I/O, and plot or explore. Reproject to a metric CRS before area, length, buffer, or distance work.
    - Declare every CRS/projection used. Use EPSG:4326 for interchange unless the solution requires another view projection, and reproject to a metric CRS before distance, area, buffer, or length calculations.
    - Specify layer order explicitly: basemap first, raster or terrain context next, polygon fills, polygon outlines, lines/routes, points/labels, then popups, tooltips, legends, controls, and diagnostics above the map.
    - Include legends for color, size, opacity, and aggregation bins; include units, classification method, source note, and missing-data treatment.
    - Include popups or tooltips with concise feature attributes, computed metrics, and keyboard or screen-reader accessible equivalents.
    - Fit the initial viewport to the provided bounds or feature group and handle resize, high-DPI, mobile/touch, and empty-data states.
    - Use high-contrast, colorblind-aware styling, semantic headings, alt or aria text for controls, visible focus states, and a tabular or textual data summary.
    - Use placeholder tokens or keys only, never print real credentials, never embed unrestricted API keys, and include a no-token-leakage diagnostic check.
    - Use deterministic inline sample data with realistic names, units, edge cases, and at least one invalid, missing, or out-of-bounds feature that is handled visibly.
    - Output only the requested source artifact with no markdown fences or explanatory prose outside the artifact.
    - Show the performance strategy in code or comments: clustering, aggregation, vector tiles, spatial index, WebGL layers, chunked analysis, workers, or sampling as appropriate.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
output:
  text_format: python
  artifact_kind: geopandas-python-analysis-asset
  formats:
    - format: python
evaluation:
  checklist:
    - "Format validity: YAML parses under schema 0.4, required fields are present, id matches the file stem, and generated output contains only the requested artifact with no markdown fences."
    - "Semantic completeness: The prompt requires native GeoPandas APIs, realistic geospatial data, scenario-specific analysis, CRS/projection handling, and no substitution with an unrelated solution."
    - "CRS/projection: Coordinates, axis order, EPSG codes, transformations, metric calculations, and projection mismatch handling are explicit and correct for the solution."
    - "Layer order: Basemap/context, polygons, outlines, routes, points, labels, controls, popups/tooltips, legends, and diagnostics are stacked deliberately and documented."
    - "Legends and source notes: Color, size, opacity, aggregation, units, classification, missing data, and data source notes are visible and understandable."
    - "Popups/tooltips: Interactive feature details expose names, metrics, units, computed values, and accessible text alternatives without occluding the map."
    - "Viewport fit: Initial camera/view/bounds frame all relevant data, with resize, mobile/touch, high-DPI, empty-data, and out-of-bounds handling."
    - "Accessibility: Headings, keyboard navigation, focus states, color contrast, non-color encodings, ARIA or textual summaries, and reduced-motion behavior are addressed."
    - "No token leakage: API keys, map tokens, service credentials, signed URLs, and secrets are placeholders only and no generated artifact prints or logs real credentials."
    - "Robustness: Missing tiles/assets, unavailable services, invalid geometries, CRS mismatches, large datasets, and offline/geofence edge cases produce visible diagnostics rather than blank output."
  rubric:
    - name: "Format validity"
      weight: 30
      criteria: "The media prompt YAML and generated artifact are syntactically valid, use schema 0.4, match the requested file/id/solution, and contain no markdown fences or malformed source."
    - name: "Semantic completeness"
      weight: 30
      criteria: "The artifact fulfills the scenario with correct solution-specific APIs, geospatial analysis, CRS/projection handling, layer order, legends, popups/tooltips, viewport fit, accessibility, and token hygiene."
    - name: "Visual/structural quality"
      weight: 25
      criteria: "The map or analysis output is legible, nonblank, well composed, colorblind-aware, appropriately annotated, and structured so data layers, controls, legends, and explanatory text do not collide."
    - name: "Robustness"
      weight: 15
      criteria: "The artifact handles missing data, invalid geometries, projection mismatches, service/token failures, offline assets, dense layers, resize/mobile behavior, and geofence edge cases with clear fallbacks."
  pass_conditions:
    - "YAML parses successfully, uses schema 0.4, and all prompt text is ASCII-only."
    - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, Visual/structural quality 25, and Robustness 15."
    - "Generated artifact uses native GeoPandas APIs and does not substitute an unrelated mapping or analysis library except for documented display/integration support."
    - "CRS/projection, layer order, legends, popups/tooltips, viewport fit, accessibility, and no token leakage checks are all satisfied."
    - "Generated artifact is nonblank, frames all relevant data on first render or first plot, and exposes diagnostics for missing services, bad geometry, empty data, or offline mode."
tags:
  - "fim"
  - "geospatial-and-mapping"
  - "geopandas"
  - "dense-layer-stress"
  - "crs"
  - "projection"
  - "legend"
  - "viewport-fit"
  - "accessibility"
  - "no-token-leakage"
  - "dense-layers"
  - "performance"
